    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d898">

                <pb facs="1273" n="1253" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg1253"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/11–2950: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Joint Chiefs of Staff to the Commander in Chief, Far
                        East</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacArthur</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">flash</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-11-29T14:30:00-05:00">29 November
                            1950—2:30 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>JCS 97592. We approve your plan in last paragraph of your C 69953<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d898-f1"/> and any directive in conflict therewith is deferred.
                    Strategic and tactical considerations are now paramount. What are your plans
                    regarding the coordination of operations of the Eighth Army and X Corps and the
                    positioning of X Corps the units of which appear to us to be exposed?</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d898-f1" n="1" xml:id="d898-f1-content">
                <p>Received at 4:46 a. m. on November 28, <ref target="#pg1237">p. 1237</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
